# Dockerfile-specific ignore file. BuildKit uses "<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore"
# next to the Dockerfile in preference to the build context root's own
# .dockerignore, when both exist. This matters here because the build
# context is the outer repository root (see the comment atop
# apps/web/Dockerfile), and that repo's own root .dockerignore is an
# allowlist tuned for its own unrelated image builds (only re-allows
# dogfood/**) — it would exclude this entire app. This file is the
# equivalent allowlist for this app instead, without touching that
# unrelated, shared file.
#
# Deny everything, then re-allow this app's own directory, then re-deny
# its build artifacts/caches so they're never sent to the Docker daemon.
**
!portfolio-command-center
!portfolio-command-center/**
portfolio-command-center/.env
portfolio-command-center/.env.local
portfolio-command-center/.env.*.local
portfolio-command-center/**/node_modules
portfolio-command-center/**/.next
portfolio-command-center/**/dist
portfolio-command-center/**/coverage
portfolio-command-center/**/.turbo
portfolio-command-center/**/*.tsbuildinfo
